  "bodyText": "Home\nVisit Us\nExhibitions\nEvents\nOnline Talks\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nCollections\nBlog\nResearch\nLearning\nShop\nCart\nMy Account\nAbout\nBecome a Friend\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\n\n01993 810 210\n\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\n  \nHome\nEvents\nExhibitions\nCollections\nFriends’ Membership\nVisit\nShop\nBasket\nMy Account\nOxfordshire’s Military Heritage in 50 Objects\nResearch\nLearning\nOnline Talks\nBlog\nSupport Us\nRoom Hire\nImage Services\nAbout\nBooks\nGifts\nChronicle of 1st Green Jackets, 43rd and 52nd and The Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry Chronicle 1959\n£5.00\n\nSorry, this item is out of stock\n\nCompiled and Edited by Lieutenant-Colonel J. B. Jarvis. Volume LXI January to December 1959.\n\nPublished 1960 - Sydney Lee (Exeter) Ltd. Hardcover.\n\n \n\nContents:\n\nThe Army List September 1959 -p.1\n\nExtracts from the 'London Gazette' -p.3\n\nRegular Officers of the Regiment Extra-Regimentally Employed -p.5\n\nFormer Officers of the Regiment on the Active List -p.6\n\n'The Chronicle' - The Editor -p.7\n\nRecords of the 1st Green Jackets, 43rd and 52nd -p.8\n\nSummary of the 1st Green Jackets, 43rd and 52nd Diary -p.10\n\nFirst Green Jackets, 43rd and 52nd Letter -p.23\n\nAddress by the Colonel of the Regiment to the 43rd and 52nd on the Occasion of His Visit to the Regiment in Cyprus, 14th March 1959 -p.29\n\nFirst Green Jackets, 43rd and 52nd, Records of Sport and Training 1958 -p.32\n\nRegimental Headquarters Letter -p.48\n\nGreen Jackets Brigade Depot Letter -p.51\n\nRecords of The Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire Light Infantry (T. A.) -p.55\n\nTerritorial Battalion Letter -p.58\n\nGreen Jackets Cricket Week 1959 -p.64\n\nThe 1st Green Jackets, 43rd and 52nd March Through Oxford -p.67\n\nThe Presentation of the Bugle Major's Stick at Bicester -p.72\n\nRegimental Dinner 1959 -p.73\n\n43rd Light Infantry Dinner (Second World War) -p.74\n\n43rd Light Infantry Mesopotamian Luncheon (First World War) -p.75\n\n52nd Light Infantry Luncheon (First World War) -p.76\n\n52nd Light Infantry Dinner (Second World War) -p.77\n\nThe Wolfe Society Dinner -p.78\n\nGroup of 52nd Officers -p.79\n\nAve Atque Vale -p.80\n\nA Visit to New Zealand -p.86\n\nDemonstration Battalion at the School of Infantry -p.88\n\nMons O.C.S.  -p.92\n\nVisit to India - December 1957 -p.95\n\nTurkish Holiday -p.100\n\nPolo -p.104\n\nFishing in Nova Scoti, 1958 -p.109\n\nSki-ing in Scotland -p.117\n\nOverland from Malta -p.120\n\nWith the French in Algeria -p.125\n\nLieut.-Colonel Sir R. G. A. Levinge, BT -p.131\n\nOld Comrades' Association 1959 -p.133\n\nMarriage -p. 1135\n\nObituaries -p.136\n\nPlease Note: Original copies supplied, all in used but reasonable condition. Copy supplied may vary slightly from the one pictured in terms of wear and aging.\n\n \n\nRelated products\nBugle & Sabre XI\n£4.99 Add to cart\nThe Royal Green Jackets Chronicle 1970\n£3.00 Add to cart\nMister Brownrigg’s Boys: Magdalen College School and the Great War\n£15.00 Add to cart\nHistory of the 43rd and 52nd (Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire) Light Infantry in the Great War 1914-1918 Volume II The 52nd Light Infantry in France and Belgium\n£30.00 Add to cart\n\nSoldiers of Oxfordshire Museum\nPark Street.\nWoodstock\nOxfordshire OX20 1SN\n\nPhone and Email:\nGeneral Enquiries & Event Tickets: 01993 810 211\nfrontofhouse@sofo.org.uk\n\nPrivacy Policy\nTerms and conditions",
